# LF EVERYWHERE, IN THE REPOSITORY AND IN THE WORKING TREE.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true at the SYSTEM level, so without
# this file a clone on Windows writes CRLF into every source file while the
# repository stores LF. That is not cosmetic here: it makes `git diff` on a
# freshly-touched file report the whole file as changed, and it makes any
# whole-file rewrite (a formatter, a sed -i, an editor "fix line endings")
# produce a 40,000-line diff that hides the two lines somebody actually meant.
#
# `eol=lf` forces the checkout as well as the commit, so every machine that
# clones this — Windows, Mac, a CI runner — has byte-identical files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The icons are the extension's toolbar mark. Marked binary explicitly so no
# future eol rule can be tempted to touch them.
*.png binary
*.crx binary
*.zip binary
